ently? Yes, the cursor is correctly drawn.\r\n - Operating system:     Ubuntu 16.04.6 LTS\r\n - Terminal emulator:    rxvt-unicode v9.22\r\n - Terminal multiplexer: tmux 2.9\r\n - `$TERM`:              tmux-256color\r\n - Shell:                zsh 5.7.1-dev-0 (x86_64-pc-linux-gnu)\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce using `nvim -u NORC`\r\n\r\nConsider this shell command:\r\n\r\n    $ nvim -Nu NONE +'colo evening'\r\n\r\n### Actual behaviour\r\n\r\nIf you type `:help` then press Tab to complete the command, the wildmenu appears and suggests:\r\n\r\n    help  helpclose  helpgrep  helptags\r\n\r\nBut the color of the cursor changes from black to light grey, and the next 2 cells are colored in white, while they should be colored like the rest of the line (i.e. dark grey).\r\nIf you insert 3 characters, the cursor color is properly restored.\r\nIf you press Tab to get the next suggestion (`helpclose`), the cursor color is, again, properly restored.\r\nIf you press Escape, the cells 5, 6 and 7 on the command-line stay in white.\r\n\r\n![gif](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/8505073/56268545-df39c200-60f1-11e9-9fa4-d99dbc8c7ade.gif)\r\n\r\nI bisected the issue to [`7ede14d`](https://github.com/neovim/neovim/commit/7ede14d191b1220ac872a24433825997d62ff7ec).\r\n\r\nIt seems related to some colorschemes, because I can't reproduce with the default one, but I can with [seoul256.vim](https://github.com/junegunn/seoul256.vim). OTOH, the terminal doesn't seem relevant, because I can reproduce in st, urxvt, xfce4-terminal and gnome-terminal, inside/outside tmux.\r\n\r\n### Expected behaviour\r\n\r\nThe cursor color should not change after tab completing `:help`.\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"justinmk","id":1359421,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNTk0MjE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1359421?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinmk","html_url":"https://github.com/justinmk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinmk/followers","